  "details": "Just like on desktop, phones have a very widely varying array of screen resolutions. My personal phone, a OnePlus 10 Pro, has a resolution of 3216 x 1440 (that's almost as high res as my desktop monitor)!\n\nBecause of this, somehigher end phones may perform WORSE than mid range phones with 1080p screens. My Snapdragon 8 Gen 1 chip runs worse in crowded instances than my Quest 2 in standalone mode, a VR headset with a much less capable chipset.\n\nBecause of this, I request the ability to change internal render resolution for VRChat Android. This would mean high end phones would be able to run the game at acceptable framerates without trying to run near 2K resolutions.",
